  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hello,\nI was thinking of simple solutions to prevent some more of the private avatar ripping I see many complain about in the community. With a safety setting, you can control who you see, how much you see, how they can communicate with you, etc.\nNow, what if we took that logic, inversed it, and had it in unity config or in the client where for private models you could hide them from anyone who is not trusted/friend in a lobby. This way the model would never be sent to other users in the lobby, not put into their cache allowing for ripping and preventing some of the issues.\nAgain this would be another band aid as I do not know if there will ever actually be a way with how computers work to fully solve this issue, but it could be another layer of safety for users with private models. \nThanks if you read this.",
